/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*-----------------------*\
  Membrane: Lab -- the BASE record of the laboratory characterisation template.

  It carries the DECLARED values; the fit operations write the records that carry the
  fitted ones (Lab_pore, Lab_X_*).  What is declared here, and only here:
    poreDielectric 53.47 the pore dielectric constant, DECLARED, not fitted.  53.47 is what
                         labban2017_dspmde_validation (op B) fitted on single-salt NaCl at
                         the isoelectric pH (+-8.8, 95 %); the article itself reports 41.3.
                         Yours comes from such a run, or from the literature of your class.
    chargeDensity 0      the start of the charge fit; X_d is fitted per concentration.
  poreRadius and porosityOverThickness are only the start of the fit (the operation's
  `initial` overrides them).  A_w is not read at an imposed flux.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------*/

name           Lab;
kind           NF;
manufacturer   "none (a laboratory membrane)";

A_w            1e-10;     // m/(s Pa), raw SI; not read at an imposed J_v

poreModel
{
    poreRadius             5.0e-10;   // m, the fit's start
    porosityOverThickness  7.5e5;     // 1/m, the fit's start
    chargeDensity          0;         // mol/m3, signed
    poreDielectric         53.47;     // -, DECLARED (see the note above)
}
